{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "01QN", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$i : Z \\to X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{I} = \\Ker(i^\\sharp)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-closed-subspace-scheme}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{schemes-definition-closed-subspace}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{schemes-example-closed-subspace}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-closed-subspace-scheme}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-closed-subspace-scheme}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0bbe4fe2f0e8b75eb62b0c1e021853c2417f0186a7b84d1bc34a30e1ad5833e2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:adc1aa3b8107516e5e97c6c2fddfebbfdc993b5861fb90749c08a7e021628da6", "source_text": "The equivalence of (1) and (2) is immediate from\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nIf (1) holds, then there is a closed subspace <MATH_0001>\nwith <MATH_0002> by\nSchemes, Definition <REF_0002>\nand Example <REF_0003>.\nBy Schemes, Lemma <REF_0004>\nthis is a closed immersion of schemes and (3) holds.\nConversely, if (3) holds, then (2) holds by\nSchemes, Lemma <REF_0005>\n(which applies because a closed immersion of schemes is a fortiori a\nclosed immersion of locally ringed spaces).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6b6e1f5e25ab0e6278fe66f09dcdb63969c196f041f3d99386944977840ac78a", "unit_id": "tag:01QQ:proof"}
